Z||000010||artherd||11-04-2001||02:45 AM||||Run 235/40/17 on the rear, it'll work fine. (215/45/17 front) 17x7 all around.   <P>It may not be totally ideal, but unless you're running a heavily modified car, it will be PLENTY of tyre. (get GOOD tyres.)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000011||Formula88||11-04-2001||02:35 PM||||Well, 235/40's would still require a minimum 8" wide wheel.  I could go wtih 235/45's on a 7.5" wide wheel, but I'd really like to get a wider wheel, even for those sizes.  I found a Racing Hart wheel that's close to what I'm looking for, except for the covered lug nuts.  I can get it in 17x9.  Now all I have to do is brace myself for how much they're gonna cost.   <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/racinghart_c2_wheel_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Rick 88||11-04-2001||05:58 PM||||I am running a 245/45/17 on the rear with 17x7.5 .40 offset wheels. The tire charts said this size is within the 7.5 in. wheel width limits. Any wider and you will have to go with at least 8 in wheels. My tires sit nice and flat across the tread on a 7.5 in wheel. <P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000013||KEV||11-04-2001||09:33 PM||||I Just installed Konig Monsoon on my 85gt the fronts are 17x7 rear 18x7.5. Tire size on front is 235 40ZR17's, rears 245 40ZR18's. They look really good on the car and clear everything. <P>------------------<BR>BLACK85GT 3800V6 2"DROP, FLUSHMOUNT HEADLIGHTS AND WRAPAROUND WING||||reg||1
